sentences.text:
This Court has considered the following facts while exercising discretion in favour of the applicant :-
(i) the applicant is in jail since 28.06.2022;
(ii) investigation is over and the charge-sheet is filed;
(iii)the applicant was already granted regular bail vide order dated 22.10.2020 passed in Criminal Misc. Application No.15510 of 2020 by the Coordinate Bench.
However, thereafter, as the present applicant could not remain present during the trial, he was arrested once again;
NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/8125/2023 ORDER DATED: 19/08/2023 undefined 6.

Hence, present application is allowed and the applicant is ordered to be released on regular bail in connection with the FIR being C.R.No.11195007200731 of 2020 registered with Bhabhar Police Station, District Banaskantha on executing personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten thousand only) with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the learned Trial Court and subject to the conditions that he shall;
[a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty;
[b] not act in a manner injuries to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;
[d] not leave India without prior permission of the Sessions Judge concerned;
[e] furnish latest address of residence to the Investigating Officer and also to the Court at the time of execution of the bond and shall not change the residence without prior permission of the trial Court;
Mukeshbhai Pachbhai Thakor vs State Of Gujarat on 19 August, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/193681902/

